WEBVTT
Kind: captions
Language: en

00:00:04.135 --> 00:00:05.377
(Cassandra sniffles)

00:00:05.377 --> 00:00:07.880
- [Mark] Cassandra, where
are you from originally?

00:00:07.880 --> 00:00:08.713
Where'd you grow up?

00:00:08.713 --> 00:00:12.623
- [Cassandra] I grew up
in Long Island, New York.

00:00:13.760 --> 00:00:15.973
- [Mark] And you grew up
with both your parents?

00:00:16.900 --> 00:00:18.810
- No, I didn't.

00:00:18.810 --> 00:00:21.530
Actually, I didn't grow up in Long Island.

00:00:21.530 --> 00:00:25.380
I was born in New York,
but I grew up in Michigan.

00:00:25.380 --> 00:00:28.000
My first, the story they
used to tell about me,

00:00:28.000 --> 00:00:31.600
my first memory was coming to find out

00:00:32.560 --> 00:00:33.970
my dad married my mom,

00:00:33.970 --> 00:00:36.890
she was pregnant with another man's kid,

00:00:36.890 --> 00:00:38.773
so I'm technically the first born.

00:00:44.150 --> 00:00:46.173
The story goes, my dad was in the Navy.

00:00:47.310 --> 00:00:50.133
He's a nuclear physicist, he
was on nuclear submarines.

00:00:51.560 --> 00:00:53.800
My mother must've been beautiful.

00:00:53.800 --> 00:00:55.230
The only thing I've been
told about her, though,

00:00:55.230 --> 00:00:57.063
is that she was stacked.

00:00:59.660 --> 00:01:03.980
But he walked away from a full
scholarship to Notre Dame.

00:01:03.980 --> 00:01:04.813
Anyway,

00:01:06.480 --> 00:01:11.400
I guess when he got off,
being away for a few months,

00:01:11.400 --> 00:01:15.070
he came to my mother's mother's house,

00:01:15.070 --> 00:01:19.130
with my mom on his arm and
my baby sister, Monique,

00:01:19.130 --> 00:01:20.840
who was three months old.

00:01:20.840 --> 00:01:22.970
His parents already had
my older sister, Dana,

00:01:22.970 --> 00:01:25.507
and said, "Mom, she cheated on me."

00:01:27.471 --> 00:01:29.820
And he left, and my mom kept me.

00:01:29.820 --> 00:01:31.663
About a year-and-a-half later,

00:01:33.530 --> 00:01:36.450
my grandparents said I was
dropped off on their doorstep

00:01:36.450 --> 00:01:41.450
in a dirty diaper with a
man's shirt on and no shoes

00:01:42.730 --> 00:01:44.360
in the middle of winter.

00:01:44.360 --> 00:01:47.830
And we had steak for dinner that night.

00:01:47.830 --> 00:01:49.903
And four hours later, we had dessert.

00:01:51.700 --> 00:01:54.080
I had something in my mouth.

00:01:54.080 --> 00:01:57.080
I had saved all my chewed up meat,

00:01:57.080 --> 00:01:58.963
because I said I wanted to eat later.

00:02:00.330 --> 00:02:03.030
I think that's the saddest
fucking story I ever heard.

00:02:03.890 --> 00:02:05.130
But they would laugh about it

00:02:05.130 --> 00:02:07.113
and tell it at the dinner table.

00:02:13.630 --> 00:02:15.793
I felt like the odd man out.

00:02:24.400 --> 00:02:25.233
I feel ...

00:02:26.911 --> 00:02:28.643
I feel guilty kind of
talking about it, you know,

00:02:31.070 --> 00:02:32.737
because I feel like,

00:02:36.649 --> 00:02:39.284
I feel guilty when talking
about why I feel guilty.

00:02:39.284 --> 00:02:40.984
But I feel like our society covets

00:02:41.890 --> 00:02:44.320
a level of attractiveness or slenderness

00:02:45.258 --> 00:02:47.263
and being the middle child.

00:02:49.600 --> 00:02:54.600
Also, I got special
treatment from strangers.

00:02:57.106 --> 00:03:01.077
And my dad, he married my
stepmother when we were,

00:03:02.451 --> 00:03:03.963
when I was six.

00:03:04.900 --> 00:03:07.480
And he married her basically
to take care of his problem,

00:03:07.480 --> 00:03:11.053
which was the three of
us, me and my two sisters.

00:03:12.090 --> 00:03:13.490
And moved us to Long Island.

00:03:15.287 --> 00:03:16.120
And I remember

00:03:20.530 --> 00:03:25.483
I was very angry at my
grandparents' house.

00:03:27.042 --> 00:03:30.513
And I kind of digress,
but after I got there,

00:03:32.150 --> 00:03:34.227
every day my grandma would tell me,

00:03:34.227 --> 00:03:35.667
"Your mom's not coming back.

00:03:35.667 --> 00:03:37.290
"She doesn't love you."

00:03:37.290 --> 00:03:39.270
And when my dad would
come home at dinner time,

00:03:39.270 --> 00:03:41.390
I had to say that my mom didn't love me,

00:03:41.390 --> 00:03:44.950
and she wasn't coming back,
and I refused to say it.

00:03:44.950 --> 00:03:46.440
So I had to go to bed without dinner,

00:03:46.440 --> 00:03:47.700
and I would get a spanking.

00:03:47.700 --> 00:03:49.453
We did this for about two years.

00:03:51.270 --> 00:03:53.530
Obviously not a good alliance to have.

00:03:53.530 --> 00:03:54.993
She never did come back.

00:03:56.380 --> 00:03:57.980
So I don't know what was worse,

00:03:57.980 --> 00:04:00.840
like the screaming for her in my head

00:04:00.840 --> 00:04:04.520
or the silence where I forgot she existed.

00:04:04.520 --> 00:04:06.683
Because silence has a sound, too.

00:04:08.050 --> 00:04:10.300
But when we moved to Long Island,

00:04:10.300 --> 00:04:13.390
Dana and Monique, they
were so traumatized,

00:04:13.390 --> 00:04:15.030
because my dad's parents

00:04:15.030 --> 00:04:17.160
were the only parents they had known.

00:04:17.160 --> 00:04:18.650
And I remember thinking to myself

00:04:18.650 --> 00:04:22.000
how lucky I was that grandma
and grandpa didn't love me,

00:04:22.000 --> 00:04:23.160
because, I mean,

00:04:24.340 --> 00:04:28.010
whether it was true or not doesn't matter.

00:04:28.010 --> 00:04:30.160
That was my feelings
about it, but I felt ...

00:04:30.160 --> 00:04:31.464
(siren wailing)
- [Mark] Give it a sec,

00:04:31.464 --> 00:04:34.534
let's let this siren go by.

00:04:34.534 --> 00:04:36.379
- Am I talking too much?

00:04:36.379 --> 00:04:38.962
(horn honking)

00:04:47.191 --> 00:04:48.921
Am I saying too much?

00:04:48.921 --> 00:04:50.088
- [Mark] No, no, you're perfect.

00:04:50.088 --> 00:04:52.210
No, I just, I wanted
to let the siren go by,

00:04:52.210 --> 00:04:54.860
because it just drowns out
whatever you're gonna say.

00:04:55.760 --> 00:04:56.710
So you were saying.

00:04:58.870 --> 00:05:00.360
- I remember thinking that,

00:05:00.360 --> 00:05:05.360
and my older sister Monique
started wetting the bed,

00:05:05.440 --> 00:05:08.480
and she would just wake up from a nap

00:05:08.480 --> 00:05:10.440
and come down to the kitchen and she'd be,

00:05:10.440 --> 00:05:12.170
tears would just be
streaming down her eyes,

00:05:12.170 --> 00:05:14.283
and she didn't even know she was crying.

00:05:17.943 --> 00:05:20.273
And that was when my
stepmom started hitting us.

00:05:21.410 --> 00:05:23.273
She would call us disgusting.

00:05:24.892 --> 00:05:26.600
And she would withhold
food as a punishment.

00:05:26.600 --> 00:05:29.870
So we would eat food out of the trash.

00:05:29.870 --> 00:05:31.620
So he were called liars and thieves

00:05:31.620 --> 00:05:32.843
when she would catch us.

00:05:35.420 --> 00:05:37.047
There's a line from a song where he says,

00:05:37.047 --> 00:05:39.967
"The reasons all have run away
but the feeling never did."

00:05:45.280 --> 00:05:48.970
So that feeling of being
guilty and unwanted,

00:05:48.970 --> 00:05:52.520
but when we were in Long Island,

00:05:52.520 --> 00:05:54.580
about two weeks, I had a dream

00:05:55.810 --> 00:05:59.537
about a guardian angel
and his name was Michael.

00:05:59.537 --> 00:06:03.380
And he said that I
wouldn't meet him again,

00:06:03.380 --> 00:06:06.980
but that I had other guardian angels

00:06:06.980 --> 00:06:09.453
and my job was to take
care of my two sisters.

00:06:10.520 --> 00:06:15.520
And that bad things were
gonna happen to me in my life.

00:06:15.570 --> 00:06:20.380
And he wanted to apologize for that,

00:06:20.380 --> 00:06:24.270
but said that God didn't
create us to make,

00:06:24.270 --> 00:06:25.930
to make us love him.

00:06:25.930 --> 00:06:28.920
So there were certain things

00:06:28.920 --> 00:06:32.473
he could control and certain
things that he couldn't.

00:06:36.820 --> 00:06:37.800
It was very vivid.

00:06:37.800 --> 00:06:39.900
I woke up my sister and told her about it.

00:06:41.590 --> 00:06:42.423
And oddly enough,

00:06:42.423 --> 00:06:45.567
one of the last things my
mother ever said to me was,

00:06:45.567 --> 00:06:48.167
"Just remember Cassie, God
shrink-wrapped your heart.

00:06:48.167 --> 00:06:50.377
"They can take everything else.

00:06:50.377 --> 00:06:53.657
"And men will touch you, but
God shrink-wrapped your heart."

00:06:56.850 --> 00:06:57.683
So.

00:07:04.766 --> 00:07:07.880
I don't know.

00:07:07.880 --> 00:07:09.180
During that period of time

00:07:12.760 --> 00:07:15.266
I didn't know my dad that well.

00:07:15.266 --> 00:07:16.223
And I wish I had.

00:07:18.360 --> 00:07:21.220
But I remember my stepmother
went back to Michigan

00:07:21.220 --> 00:07:25.300
for a couple of days and my
father was left to care for us.

00:07:25.300 --> 00:07:28.300
Now he had me when he was 20.

00:07:28.300 --> 00:07:32.040
So you can imagine he was a young man.

00:07:32.040 --> 00:07:35.910
And he would have been,
what, 25 at this time?

00:07:35.910 --> 00:07:38.880
But we were playing on the floor.

00:07:38.880 --> 00:07:39.713
It was one of the first times

00:07:39.713 --> 00:07:41.797
I really spent time with him alone.

00:07:41.797 --> 00:07:43.700
And I remember he pinched me so hard

00:07:43.700 --> 00:07:47.480
that it left like a blood blister.

00:07:47.480 --> 00:07:48.890
I felt so offended.

00:07:48.890 --> 00:07:50.003
It was such a strange thing.

00:07:50.003 --> 00:07:51.770
It's a strange story to tell.

00:07:51.770 --> 00:07:54.120
But after that, I kind
of stayed away from him.

00:07:59.953 --> 00:08:01.000
We got hit every day.

00:08:01.000 --> 00:08:03.960
My step mom started having her own kids.

00:08:03.960 --> 00:08:08.960
And Dana and Monique were
increasingly called fat and ugly.

00:08:09.280 --> 00:08:11.160
We weren't allowed to go
in the store with her,

00:08:11.160 --> 00:08:15.000
because we were, she was too
beautiful to have children

00:08:15.000 --> 00:08:17.033
like us or as old as us.

00:08:20.680 --> 00:08:22.683
And when we moved back to Michigan.

00:08:27.210 --> 00:08:28.100
I try not,

00:08:28.100 --> 00:08:30.220
I always say that I,

00:08:30.220 --> 00:08:32.360
and I'm not mad, but I
don't think about it.

00:08:32.360 --> 00:08:34.680
I won't think about it
longer than five seconds.

00:08:34.680 --> 00:08:37.723
My two sisters, they hate
and they hate beautifully.

00:08:39.190 --> 00:08:41.333
They're married.

00:08:42.620 --> 00:08:44.270
They have good lives.

00:08:44.270 --> 00:08:48.170
My older sister has two master's degrees.

00:08:48.170 --> 00:08:49.240
My younger sister got accepted

00:08:49.240 --> 00:08:50.883
to all these amazing colleges.

00:08:53.040 --> 00:08:57.400
But it's a daily thing where
they speak about our childhood

00:08:58.590 --> 00:09:01.483
and blame them singularly.

00:09:02.500 --> 00:09:03.450
That doesn't work for me.

00:09:03.450 --> 00:09:05.893
I find it's hard to sustain.

00:09:11.090 --> 00:09:16.090
If I think about it longer than 30 seconds

00:09:17.162 --> 00:09:18.890
the rage is so intense.

00:09:18.890 --> 00:09:23.890
I just, I think, I can't handle it.

00:09:25.300 --> 00:09:26.460
You know, I was 13-and-a-half.

00:09:26.460 --> 00:09:28.490
My dad was arrested for child abuse

00:09:29.510 --> 00:09:31.543
against me specifically.

00:09:33.130 --> 00:09:38.130
And you know, my stepmother had been the,

00:09:39.070 --> 00:09:42.193
she broke my older
sister's nose four times.

00:09:42.193 --> 00:09:44.633
Food was always withheld as a punishment.

00:09:46.890 --> 00:09:48.210
I used to have to take my clothes off

00:09:48.210 --> 00:09:50.970
before I left for school
and when I came back.

00:09:50.970 --> 00:09:53.250
I mean, she would physically put

00:09:53.250 --> 00:09:54.480
her fingers inside me to see

00:09:54.480 --> 00:09:56.913
if I had taken, was
bringing anything home.

00:09:58.120 --> 00:10:00.773
I got a candy bar wrapper or ...

00:10:06.200 --> 00:10:08.393
So my father took her to trial.

00:10:10.540 --> 00:10:15.540
That day they estimated
he hit me about 60 times

00:10:16.060 --> 00:10:18.080
with the buckle end of a belt,

00:10:18.080 --> 00:10:20.580
and then an hour-and-a-half
went by and he was still mad.

00:10:20.580 --> 00:10:25.580
So he did it another 50
times, shattered my tailbone.

00:10:25.760 --> 00:10:28.330
That night my clothes scabbed to me,

00:10:28.330 --> 00:10:30.110
but I didn't cry

00:10:31.150 --> 00:10:32.957
until I collapsed on the floor and said,

00:10:32.957 --> 00:10:34.417
"Please don't hit me again."

00:10:35.426 --> 00:10:36.726
It's just so embarrassing.

00:10:40.860 --> 00:10:41.737
And he said, "I'm gonna hit you

00:10:41.737 --> 00:10:43.887
"like this every day
that you're grounded."

00:10:45.190 --> 00:10:47.930
So I ran away that night

00:10:49.460 --> 00:10:50.607
and I went to school for the first time,

00:10:50.607 --> 00:10:52.270
I went to school the next day.

00:10:52.270 --> 00:10:54.253
I never missed a day of school.

00:10:56.250 --> 00:10:58.990
My principal said, "You're
not allowed to be here."

00:10:58.990 --> 00:10:59.970
He had called the police.

00:10:59.970 --> 00:11:01.680
I was so terrified.

00:11:01.680 --> 00:11:03.313
He said I'd get in so much trouble.

00:11:06.050 --> 00:11:07.390
They were gonna relinquish me to him,

00:11:07.390 --> 00:11:10.983
but a female teacher
demanded a female officer.

00:11:12.520 --> 00:11:13.900
I didn't make a statement.

00:11:13.900 --> 00:11:17.630
I never told, but the
injuries spoke for themselves.

00:11:17.630 --> 00:11:18.793
He took it to trial.

00:11:27.290 --> 00:11:29.690
The day of the trial he
asked me to lie for him.

00:11:32.030 --> 00:11:34.300
They ended up keeping me in the house.

00:11:34.300 --> 00:11:35.550
They sent me to live with

00:11:36.570 --> 00:11:38.040
my grandfather who said

00:11:38.040 --> 00:11:40.420
I was a whore and couldn't stay there.

00:11:40.420 --> 00:11:44.233
And, but the day of the trial,

00:11:45.385 --> 00:11:47.890
in the cafeteria the family's on one side,

00:11:47.890 --> 00:11:49.570
me and him are on the other.

00:11:49.570 --> 00:11:50.423
And he says,

00:11:51.840 --> 00:11:54.670
how do I feel about
destroying everybody's life?

00:11:54.670 --> 00:11:56.240
And that he was gonna go to jail?

00:11:56.240 --> 00:11:58.907
And I said, "How does it
feel to have your freedom

00:11:58.907 --> 00:12:01.807
"in the hands of somebody that
you said was so worthless?"

00:12:03.366 --> 00:12:05.543
That's one of the things
I'm most proud of,

00:12:06.390 --> 00:12:11.390
that I had the wherewithal
to know to say that.

00:12:13.806 --> 00:12:16.410
If I ever feel bad, I can remember that.

00:12:16.410 --> 00:12:18.004
And I did lie for him.

00:12:18.004 --> 00:12:19.093
(sirens wailing)

00:12:19.093 --> 00:12:20.553
- [Mark] Just let the siren go by.

00:12:24.410 --> 00:12:25.890
Yep, they stopped.

00:12:27.580 --> 00:12:30.030
- One thing though, I had a
severe stuttering problem.

00:12:30.030 --> 00:12:32.850
It started when I was about six years old.

00:12:32.850 --> 00:12:33.840
Very, very bad.

00:12:33.840 --> 00:12:35.270
Most people don't know this about me.

00:12:35.270 --> 00:12:36.103
Really bad.

00:12:36.103 --> 00:12:37.097
Every word, duh-duh-duh.

00:12:39.070 --> 00:12:40.373
It was incapacitating.

00:12:42.350 --> 00:12:45.420
And when I had to, this is
when they put me on the stand,

00:12:45.420 --> 00:12:46.673
I couldn't say my name.

00:12:48.700 --> 00:12:50.300
Now as an adult, I go by Cassandra,

00:12:50.300 --> 00:12:51.750
but I couldn't say Cassandra.

00:12:52.640 --> 00:12:53.497
I could only say Cassie

00:12:53.497 --> 00:12:56.564
and I was supposed to state
my full name for the court.

00:12:56.564 --> 00:12:58.350
And the judge was a female.

00:12:58.350 --> 00:12:59.183
And she said,

00:12:59.183 --> 00:13:01.604
"I can't believe you're
gonna put her through this.

00:13:01.604 --> 00:13:04.100
"Quietly just accept the plea bargain."

00:13:04.100 --> 00:13:08.223
But I did lie for him
and I left the next day.

00:13:09.230 --> 00:13:11.240
I've never been back.

00:13:11.240 --> 00:13:12.760
But after I left ...

00:13:12.760 --> 00:13:14.283
- [Mark] Just let this go by.

00:13:16.447 --> 00:13:19.640
- I have to say, I had a social worker.

00:13:19.640 --> 00:13:20.490
Can I say her name?

00:13:20.490 --> 00:13:22.140
Janine McFarlane.
- [Mark] Sure.

00:13:23.220 --> 00:13:24.270
- She was so amazing.

00:13:24.270 --> 00:13:25.763
This is in Detroit, you know?

00:13:28.786 --> 00:13:31.370
And she found me, Janine found me,

00:13:31.370 --> 00:13:35.980
until I was 30 years old and
she would send me a gift.

00:13:35.980 --> 00:13:37.340
I mean, we're talking,

00:13:37.340 --> 00:13:39.980
she showed up in like three
carat diamond earrings

00:13:39.980 --> 00:13:41.630
and a mink coat and drove a Mercedes.

00:13:41.630 --> 00:13:42.903
Very unusual.

00:13:46.900 --> 00:13:51.780
When I was 15 I was bullied
really bad in school.

00:13:51.780 --> 00:13:53.480
Really, really bad.

00:13:53.480 --> 00:13:55.310
In fact, I came to a
point before the trial

00:13:55.310 --> 00:13:56.810
where I stopped seeing colors.

00:13:57.760 --> 00:13:58.963
I was really scared.

00:14:02.880 --> 00:14:05.560
I was left for dead in
the snow by two girls.

00:14:05.560 --> 00:14:07.060
They put cigarettes out on me.

00:14:10.030 --> 00:14:12.210
I would say the quickest
way to sober me up

00:14:12.210 --> 00:14:14.310
is put me in a room with fucked up people.

00:14:16.670 --> 00:14:17.720
The worst thing I could think of to do

00:14:17.720 --> 00:14:19.920
to say I was upset was smoke cigarettes,

00:14:19.920 --> 00:14:22.338
but I remember I grew up in

00:14:22.338 --> 00:14:24.393
a good neighborhood, if you will,

00:14:25.400 --> 00:14:27.040
But the kids who were on the
wrong side of the tracks,

00:14:27.040 --> 00:14:28.363
their parents didn't ask,

00:14:29.307 --> 00:14:31.707
"Why is this girl here on a school night?"

00:14:32.840 --> 00:14:37.240
But I have no idea why I got so fortunate.

00:14:37.240 --> 00:14:38.550
I knew there were drugs all around,

00:14:38.550 --> 00:14:43.063
but I didn't see them and
I stayed away from them.

00:14:44.960 --> 00:14:48.733
But somebody's trashy
mother called somebody's,

00:14:50.490 --> 00:14:51.620
some of these girls, girl,

00:14:51.620 --> 00:14:56.620
that I was with this boy.

00:14:57.210 --> 00:15:02.210
And I had yet to even
get that far with a boy.

00:15:04.730 --> 00:15:07.060
But a group of people came

00:15:07.060 --> 00:15:11.850
and three girls beat me up.

00:15:11.850 --> 00:15:14.400
And they took all my clothes,
put cigarettes out on me.

00:15:14.400 --> 00:15:18.210
When I came to, they said,
"The street's that way."

00:15:18.210 --> 00:15:19.913
I knocked on seven doors.

00:15:21.410 --> 00:15:24.410
It was about 7:30 at night
before someone opened the door.

00:15:24.410 --> 00:15:25.740
- [Mark] How old were you?

00:15:25.740 --> 00:15:26.573
- 15.

00:15:31.250 --> 00:15:34.850
And I just remember coming
in and out of consciousness,

00:15:34.850 --> 00:15:36.370
bleeding all over this,

00:15:36.370 --> 00:15:38.800
yeah, it was a young couple,
all over their bathroom.

00:15:38.800 --> 00:15:41.440
And I kept saying, "I'm
really not white trash."

00:15:41.440 --> 00:15:43.334
And then my dad was in the doorway.

00:15:43.334 --> 00:15:45.200
I said, "How did you know who my dad was?"

00:15:45.200 --> 00:15:46.650
And they said, "You told us."

00:15:47.610 --> 00:15:49.410
After they put me back in the house,

00:15:51.460 --> 00:15:52.660
no one was allowed to call me Cassie,

00:15:52.660 --> 00:15:54.940
everybody had to call me Stupid.

00:15:54.940 --> 00:15:56.870
I was no longer a part of the family.

00:15:56.870 --> 00:15:57.703
The hitting stopped,

00:15:57.703 --> 00:16:00.163
but it was on, it was a war.

00:16:01.460 --> 00:16:05.100
And Dana and Monique,
they got it the worst.

00:16:05.100 --> 00:16:06.453
Dana got it really bad.

00:16:07.330 --> 00:16:08.533
I'd been beat up.

00:16:09.720 --> 00:16:11.930
I remember, my parents
rarely ever went out,

00:16:11.930 --> 00:16:14.743
but the Christmas cookie story.

00:16:15.970 --> 00:16:19.360
They went out during the holidays once

00:16:19.360 --> 00:16:21.260
and we never had house keys,

00:16:21.260 --> 00:16:22.570
we were not allowed to open the fridge

00:16:22.570 --> 00:16:26.333
or touch the television
or the radio, nothing.

00:16:27.480 --> 00:16:28.540
We didn't have keys to the house,

00:16:28.540 --> 00:16:30.090
because remember we
were liars and thieves,

00:16:30.090 --> 00:16:31.840
we might eat food.

00:16:31.840 --> 00:16:33.490
So we're waiting in the garage,

00:16:33.490 --> 00:16:34.510
when we come home from school

00:16:34.510 --> 00:16:38.967
and on the door to the garage
leading into the house is,

00:16:38.967 --> 00:16:39.910
"Use guys."

00:16:39.910 --> 00:16:41.297
My stepmother would use that word.

00:16:41.297 --> 00:16:43.167
"Better get your story straight.

00:16:43.167 --> 00:16:45.037
"There were 32 Christmas cookies.

00:16:45.037 --> 00:16:49.083
"And then when we got home
last night, there were 22.

00:16:51.017 --> 00:16:52.527
"Somebody's gonna get it.

00:16:52.527 --> 00:16:57.130
"You better, whoever did it,
you know, better step forth."

00:16:57.130 --> 00:16:59.510
Dana starts wailing like, "Oh God!"

00:16:59.510 --> 00:17:00.343
You know?

00:17:01.600 --> 00:17:03.223
And I remember saying, "Okay, okay.

00:17:03.223 --> 00:17:04.547
"It's almost like Ferris
Bueller's day off, right?

00:17:04.547 --> 00:17:05.607
"I'll take the heat."

00:17:06.920 --> 00:17:10.940
My stepmother, that Air
Star minivan pulls up.

00:17:10.940 --> 00:17:12.890
She doesn't ask who did it.

00:17:12.890 --> 00:17:13.850
She just gets out.

00:17:13.850 --> 00:17:16.493
She grabs Dana by the hair
and takes her to the kitchen.

00:17:16.493 --> 00:17:18.850
And she starts banging her
head against the stove.

00:17:18.850 --> 00:17:20.930
I'm terrified.

00:17:20.930 --> 00:17:22.580
And that's when I realized,

00:17:22.580 --> 00:17:24.980
it didn't have to do with
the Christmas cookies.

00:17:25.980 --> 00:17:27.280
It was just rage,

00:17:27.280 --> 00:17:29.900
she wanted to take it out on anyone.

00:17:29.900 --> 00:17:32.540
I remember running to
the phone and saying,

00:17:32.540 --> 00:17:33.857
I thought she was going to kill Dana,

00:17:33.857 --> 00:17:35.500
"I'm gonna call 911!"

00:17:35.500 --> 00:17:37.290
My stepmother just grabbed the phone

00:17:37.290 --> 00:17:38.963
out of my hand and hit me over
the head with it and said,

00:17:38.963 --> 00:17:40.647
"You're not calling anyone."

00:17:42.770 --> 00:17:44.120
That was a valuable lesson.

00:17:47.070 --> 00:17:48.910
My two sisters,

00:17:48.910 --> 00:17:50.710
no one grows up wanting to be a liar

00:17:52.001 --> 00:17:56.563
or a drug addict or promiscuous.

00:17:58.210 --> 00:18:01.050
But I don't, I mean, I feel fortunate.

00:18:01.050 --> 00:18:02.563
I learned very early on that,

00:18:03.690 --> 00:18:05.560
the goalposts were constantly changing.

00:18:05.560 --> 00:18:10.560
And I was taught how to be a good liar.

00:18:11.680 --> 00:18:13.940
I likened my stepmother to,

00:18:13.940 --> 00:18:16.333
I got big ogre.

00:18:17.997 --> 00:18:21.423
And you could see when
the rage would start.

00:18:23.557 --> 00:18:25.977
"Who was in the refrigerator,

00:18:25.977 --> 00:18:28.580
"or who didn't take out the trash?"

00:18:28.580 --> 00:18:31.350
If you went to the
bathroom or left number two

00:18:31.350 --> 00:18:33.790
you'd have to go into the bathroom

00:18:33.790 --> 00:18:36.650
and stand there until
someone said, "Who did it?"

00:18:36.650 --> 00:18:39.743
For hours, like why not
just flush the toilet?

00:18:41.263 --> 00:18:43.110
I mean, I don't know
what any of this means.

00:18:43.110 --> 00:18:45.893
I've never revisited this.

00:18:47.640 --> 00:18:50.480
But if you lied to my stepmother

00:18:50.480 --> 00:18:55.480
then the momentum of the
punch wouldn't be as,

00:18:56.740 --> 00:18:59.380
it wouldn't hurt as bad.

00:18:59.380 --> 00:19:00.590
If you were like, "Look over there."

00:19:00.590 --> 00:19:01.465
You know?

00:19:01.465 --> 00:19:03.610
It would confuse her almost.

00:19:03.610 --> 00:19:04.443
So.

00:19:06.248 --> 00:19:07.081
And if you recall,

00:19:07.081 --> 00:19:10.840
I had a different father
than my older sister, Dana.

00:19:10.840 --> 00:19:13.950
There's a picture of us,
even though we're almost,

00:19:13.950 --> 00:19:16.700
Dana, my older sister is
almost exactly a year older

00:19:16.700 --> 00:19:18.490
and my little one, almost
exactly a year younger.

00:19:18.490 --> 00:19:19.740
And we all shared a room.

00:19:20.640 --> 00:19:23.320
But in this photograph,

00:19:23.320 --> 00:19:28.070
I am up to Dana's shoulder
and she has her arm around me.

00:19:28.070 --> 00:19:31.000
Dana was much larger than me,

00:19:31.000 --> 00:19:35.680
but more of a gentle soul and
more fearful, anxiety ridden.

00:19:35.680 --> 00:19:39.060
I would say when, and
Dana would go for her.

00:19:39.060 --> 00:19:40.300
We'd say, "Dana, hit her back."

00:19:40.300 --> 00:19:41.800
We just weren't big enough.

00:19:41.800 --> 00:19:42.633
You know?

00:19:42.633 --> 00:19:43.500
Dana was like 5'11.

00:19:43.500 --> 00:19:44.933
She'd be terrifying today.

00:19:48.360 --> 00:19:52.280
But what was I saying?

00:19:52.280 --> 00:19:55.270
- [Mark] You mentioned earlier
on before we started cameras,

00:19:55.270 --> 00:19:56.900
that you were molested at some point?

00:19:56.900 --> 00:19:57.932
- Yes.

00:19:57.932 --> 00:19:59.632
After I left home after the trial,

00:20:01.540 --> 00:20:04.030
I didn't have a winter coat

00:20:04.030 --> 00:20:06.470
and I would sit in the
breezeway of this restaurant.

00:20:06.470 --> 00:20:08.850
After about a month a man
gave me a roll of dimes

00:20:08.850 --> 00:20:10.120
and said to call someone.

00:20:10.120 --> 00:20:11.517
I looked in the yellow pages for my aunt,

00:20:11.517 --> 00:20:13.583
and I remember my mother's maiden name.

00:20:14.430 --> 00:20:16.893
And I found her sister
who came and picked me up.

00:20:18.825 --> 00:20:19.658
The first thing she asked was

00:20:19.658 --> 00:20:21.580
"What kind of cigarettes do you smoke?"

00:20:21.580 --> 00:20:23.390
And I hadn't really learned how to inhale,

00:20:23.390 --> 00:20:25.190
but I just looked down and
she smoked Virginia Slims.

00:20:25.190 --> 00:20:27.240
And as I said, "I smoke those."

00:20:27.240 --> 00:20:28.073
She said, "What a coincidence."

00:20:28.073 --> 00:20:30.000
And went and got me a pack.

00:20:30.000 --> 00:20:31.150
They were drug addicts.

00:20:32.150 --> 00:20:33.037
- [Mark] How old were you?

00:20:33.037 --> 00:20:35.563
- Almost 16, 15-and-a-half.

00:20:35.563 --> 00:20:36.396
- [Mark] Okay.

00:20:36.396 --> 00:20:39.700
- She had a son, he was 20 years older.

00:20:39.700 --> 00:20:41.540
He was my cousin, I never met him,

00:20:41.540 --> 00:20:43.040
but she put me in his bedroom.

00:20:44.980 --> 00:20:46.900
I thought she didn't know.

00:20:46.900 --> 00:20:48.680
But now I realize she
put me in his bedroom

00:20:48.680 --> 00:20:50.330
so he'd come home with the drugs.

00:20:52.110 --> 00:20:55.657
And it was, "You do, as we
do, or you don't stay here."

00:21:00.670 --> 00:21:02.560
I mean, it's hard to express.

00:21:02.560 --> 00:21:03.393
It's hard.

00:21:03.393 --> 00:21:06.540
It's hard to draw a picture,

00:21:06.540 --> 00:21:09.473
but we had no furniture,
much like crackheads.

00:21:10.800 --> 00:21:13.210
My cousin was a gaffer.

00:21:13.210 --> 00:21:16.910
So I always slept on the floor.

00:21:16.910 --> 00:21:21.080
We had a spool as our coffee
table and director's chairs.

00:21:21.080 --> 00:21:22.830
And then we had a chalkboard

00:21:22.830 --> 00:21:25.450
to keep track of anybody who double toked.

00:21:25.450 --> 00:21:26.373
This is pot.

00:21:28.920 --> 00:21:32.350
We had a SWAT team come
into her house actually.

00:21:32.350 --> 00:21:34.200
But that first night that I was there

00:21:35.090 --> 00:21:36.533
on the floor in his bedroom,

00:21:37.520 --> 00:21:39.750
my cousin got out of his bed

00:21:39.750 --> 00:21:42.223
and laid down next to me behind me.

00:21:46.161 --> 00:21:47.620
I still had never, I mean,

00:21:47.620 --> 00:21:51.730
the most I had done was kiss a boy.

00:21:51.730 --> 00:21:52.633
So.

00:21:54.560 --> 00:21:55.800
He took my choice to choose.

00:21:55.800 --> 00:22:00.180
He didn't, he didn't do it that night.

00:22:00.180 --> 00:22:01.323
He was ...

00:22:07.670 --> 00:22:10.663
As far as predators
go, he made it seem ...

00:22:13.150 --> 00:22:16.013
I lie to myself as if I
was a participant in it.

00:22:24.230 --> 00:22:25.860
It changes things.

00:22:25.860 --> 00:22:27.910
This is really hard for me to talk about.

00:22:29.240 --> 00:22:30.340
And it's really scary.

00:22:33.800 --> 00:22:37.913
I guess it creates certain
proclivities in your life.

00:22:41.570 --> 00:22:42.697
I'm not gonna explain what that means,

00:22:42.697 --> 00:22:45.360
but I'm sure you can look up the word.

00:22:45.360 --> 00:22:48.457
- [Mark] Okay, you don't want
to talk about it, all right.

00:22:50.150 --> 00:22:53.000
- I guess, I just, he took
what he took and I didn't want

00:22:53.900 --> 00:22:55.650
to be, to sit at that bus stop

00:22:55.650 --> 00:22:57.400
like a survivor of being molested.

00:22:57.400 --> 00:22:59.053
So I just told myself some story.

00:23:00.900 --> 00:23:03.230
But then I was off to the races,

00:23:03.230 --> 00:23:05.100
I became a pot addict.

00:23:05.100 --> 00:23:06.750
That's an underrated addiction.

00:23:06.750 --> 00:23:09.370
I smoked pot every day for five years.

00:23:09.370 --> 00:23:10.320
I'll tell you what.

00:23:15.050 --> 00:23:18.320
And like I said, God was my only friend.

00:23:18.320 --> 00:23:20.740
So I cried myself to sleep

00:23:20.740 --> 00:23:24.823
for maybe two years
wanting to get out and ...

00:23:26.920 --> 00:23:28.244
Could we take a break?

00:23:28.244 --> 00:23:29.077
- [Mark] Sure.

00:23:29.077 --> 00:23:29.910
- Sorry.

00:23:32.036 --> 00:23:36.330
Okay, I guess, I didn't tell my aunt.

00:23:36.330 --> 00:23:40.883
I felt like that, you
know, just to protect her.

00:23:44.470 --> 00:23:46.350
I hadn't smoked pot before.

00:23:46.350 --> 00:23:49.093
And I remember telling a girl next door

00:23:49.093 --> 00:23:52.230
after two weeks of being there,
"I can't keep doing this."

00:23:52.230 --> 00:23:53.550
You know?

00:23:53.550 --> 00:23:56.880
Come to find out my aunt
had taken my dad to court

00:23:56.880 --> 00:23:58.420
and she was getting money from him.

00:23:58.420 --> 00:24:00.970
She never so much as bought
me a pair of underwear.

00:24:04.140 --> 00:24:06.547
She, at first she told me,

00:24:06.547 --> 00:24:09.017
"You're not going to school anymore.

00:24:09.017 --> 00:24:11.060
"You're gonna watch Dylan."

00:24:11.060 --> 00:24:14.743
Which is my cousin's son, who was seven.

00:24:16.550 --> 00:24:18.670
I went, we got evicted from every place.

00:24:18.670 --> 00:24:22.200
So went from an upscale neighborhood to

00:24:22.200 --> 00:24:23.950
basically the Skid Row of Michigan.

00:24:25.690 --> 00:24:27.893
We ended up in Redford Union, Eight Mile.

00:24:31.115 --> 00:24:33.623
There was a shower downstairs

00:24:33.623 --> 00:24:35.770
in one of the places that we rented.

00:24:35.770 --> 00:24:37.290
It was an unfinished basement,

00:24:37.290 --> 00:24:38.930
and I'll never forget this.

00:24:38.930 --> 00:24:41.220
I came downstairs and
I hear my little cousin

00:24:41.220 --> 00:24:44.297
who's eight years old
saying, sobbing, going,

00:24:44.297 --> 00:24:46.600
"Why me, God, why me?"

00:24:46.600 --> 00:24:47.653
In the shower.

00:24:54.530 --> 00:24:59.530
I did, prior to her
pulling me out of school.

00:25:00.030 --> 00:25:02.220
I did end up going to high school

00:25:02.220 --> 00:25:03.600
for about three weeks at a place,

00:25:03.600 --> 00:25:06.823
at a high school called
Redford Union on Eight Mile.

00:25:07.800 --> 00:25:09.563
Yes, where Eminem hails from.

00:25:11.350 --> 00:25:13.640
And two events happened.

00:25:18.530 --> 00:25:20.650
I ended up meeting the
cutest boy in school

00:25:20.650 --> 00:25:22.680
whose girlfriend was on a family vacation,

00:25:22.680 --> 00:25:24.180
but no one thought to tell me.

00:25:26.530 --> 00:25:31.530
And the principal there,
he had me in his office

00:25:34.080 --> 00:25:37.313
and he asked me to
unbutton my shirt for him.

00:25:39.740 --> 00:25:43.100
And that stayed with me forever

00:25:44.280 --> 00:25:46.550
for a number of reasons.

00:25:46.550 --> 00:25:49.780
That wasn't in my file anything about me,

00:25:49.780 --> 00:25:52.243
about sexual abuse.

00:25:53.130 --> 00:25:55.583
How did he know that I wouldn't tell?

00:25:59.470 --> 00:26:01.283
From then on I felt like everybody knew,

00:26:01.283 --> 00:26:02.910
like I was wearing a scarlet letter.

00:26:02.910 --> 00:26:06.223
Everybody knew that I was being molested.

00:26:08.530 --> 00:26:09.503
And ...

00:26:13.840 --> 00:26:14.810
This is only one of the few times

00:26:14.810 --> 00:26:16.570
in my life I've ever vocalized that

00:26:19.100 --> 00:26:20.307
or allowed myself to.

00:26:20.307 --> 00:26:22.543
I'm a very compartmentalized person.

00:26:24.020 --> 00:26:27.300
And I don't consider myself a liar.

00:26:27.300 --> 00:26:30.610
And if I ever do lie, it's because I'm,

00:26:30.610 --> 00:26:33.423
I've probably lied to myself as well.

00:26:34.640 --> 00:26:39.640
But how could he have
known I wouldn't tell?

00:26:39.980 --> 00:26:41.723
And did I comply?
Yes.

00:26:44.781 --> 00:26:47.963
I found power from it in a way.

00:26:50.360 --> 00:26:51.651
On the flip side,

00:26:51.651 --> 00:26:56.651
the downside was a billion miles deep,

00:26:58.950 --> 00:27:01.653
but after ...

00:27:03.130 --> 00:27:06.510
I felt like I had no choice, so I made it,

00:27:06.510 --> 00:27:09.770
I lied to myself as if
I did in the moment.

00:27:09.770 --> 00:27:12.077
And what I was telling myself was,

00:27:12.077 --> 00:27:14.657
"So dad, you said I was so worthless.

00:27:14.657 --> 00:27:15.637
"Well, guess what?

00:27:15.637 --> 00:27:18.873
"I can make this person risk everything.

00:27:20.127 --> 00:27:21.440
"So how worthless am I

00:27:23.627 --> 00:27:25.827
"if I can bring this
person to their knees?"

00:27:30.800 --> 00:27:34.710
Whatever somebody thinks of that

00:27:35.760 --> 00:27:37.060
is neither here nor there.

00:27:38.840 --> 00:27:39.890
It is what it is

00:27:42.710 --> 00:27:44.203
as far as then.

00:27:45.520 --> 00:27:47.920
And I maybe only know
this now, looking back

00:27:47.920 --> 00:27:52.920
but after Mauritzio,
his girlfriend got back,

00:27:54.680 --> 00:27:57.290
we were living of course, renting a place

00:27:57.290 --> 00:27:59.193
made out of Kleenex and spit.

00:28:00.040 --> 00:28:04.513
There was maybe 40 girls
outside calling for my head.

00:28:06.760 --> 00:28:07.640
Terrifying.

00:28:07.640 --> 00:28:10.380
So, no, I never went back
to school after that.

00:28:10.380 --> 00:28:12.370
But I did have one friend, Tamara,

00:28:12.370 --> 00:28:13.540
who worked at Taco Bell.

00:28:13.540 --> 00:28:16.850
Shortly thereafter the SWAT
team came into our house.

00:28:16.850 --> 00:28:20.860
My cousin Dylan was selling
pot out of the house.

00:28:20.860 --> 00:28:23.960
My aunt would send me with
him to the tip of Florida,

00:28:23.960 --> 00:28:27.133
where we would drive there
and back in three days.

00:28:28.320 --> 00:28:32.020
He would put the bricks of
marijuana above the engine.

00:28:32.020 --> 00:28:33.593
He would use a gaffers blanket.

00:28:37.830 --> 00:28:40.760
Yeah, so when the SWAT team came in,

00:28:40.760 --> 00:28:42.840
you know, "Get down, get down, get down!"

00:28:42.840 --> 00:28:45.910
His girlfriend, Tamara,
she was about 350 pounds

00:28:45.910 --> 00:28:47.830
and she worked at Taco Bell.

00:28:47.830 --> 00:28:49.440
The police kept calling
her the Big Burrito.

00:28:49.440 --> 00:28:51.360
She's like, she wasn't gonna get down,

00:28:51.360 --> 00:28:56.360
but they took us all to jail

00:28:56.410 --> 00:28:58.890
and then they proceeded to tell me that

00:28:58.890 --> 00:29:03.420
if I didn't buy drugs from three people

00:29:03.420 --> 00:29:05.510
three times with marked money,

00:29:05.510 --> 00:29:06.710
I was gonna go to prison.

00:29:06.710 --> 00:29:08.963
They had photographs
of me opening the door.

00:29:12.490 --> 00:29:14.003
Wow, this is so embarrassing.

00:29:16.190 --> 00:29:21.190
I, when I was 13-and-a-half,
when ninth grade first started,

00:29:25.120 --> 00:29:26.910
you were allowed to
leave campus for school.

00:29:26.910 --> 00:29:29.560
And there was this man, Todd Caribbean.

00:29:29.560 --> 00:29:31.430
He was probably 36 years old,

00:29:31.430 --> 00:29:34.050
but he would hang outside the pizza place.

00:29:34.050 --> 00:29:36.940
And some of my girlfriends knew him.

00:29:36.940 --> 00:29:39.563
Of course the girls from the
wrong side of the tracks.

00:29:41.310 --> 00:29:45.540
But he, when I would run away from home,

00:29:45.540 --> 00:29:48.673
he would put me in a hotel room.

00:29:50.230 --> 00:29:54.223
But so when I had to buy
these drugs with marked money,

00:29:55.700 --> 00:29:58.590
I bought drugs from friends of his

00:29:58.590 --> 00:30:00.760
that weren't really drug dealers.

