00:45:12.800 --> 00:45:14.300
Maybe he didn't like where I chose to sit,

00:45:14.300 --> 00:45:19.300
but I said, "You know, I
can't see myself drinking,

00:45:21.587 --> 00:45:24.747
"but if I do, I'm very
concerned about having seizures.

00:45:24.747 --> 00:45:28.620
"What, if anything, can you
give me to prevent that?"

00:45:28.620 --> 00:45:30.237
He said, "Well, first of all

00:45:30.237 --> 00:45:32.677
"I think you need a 12 step program.

00:45:32.677 --> 00:45:35.807
"And secondly, I think
you sexualize situations

00:45:35.807 --> 00:45:37.397
"and probably always will."

00:45:42.950 --> 00:45:46.630
Even as I speak it, I
can hardly believe it.

00:45:46.630 --> 00:45:48.184
What is that?

00:45:48.184 --> 00:45:52.947
It took me a decade-and-a-half
to convince myself that,

00:45:52.947 --> 00:45:56.417
"No one can tell that you
were molested, Cassie.

00:45:56.417 --> 00:45:58.547
"You know, it's just in your head."

00:45:59.430 --> 00:46:04.390
The two or three people I
ever told about it, you know,

00:46:04.390 --> 00:46:08.160
had close, close friends,
had convinced me of the same.

00:46:08.160 --> 00:46:11.383
And I was just starting to kind
of move forward in my life.

00:46:14.975 --> 00:46:17.773
And that kind of tore all that down.

00:46:20.290 --> 00:46:24.660
But right now, this conversation
is neither here nor there.

00:46:24.660 --> 00:46:26.230
About two months later,

00:46:26.230 --> 00:46:28.640
I finished everything I
needed to do for the DUI.

00:46:28.640 --> 00:46:31.100
Mind you, the classes
were at 8:30 at night

00:46:31.100 --> 00:46:32.300
and that was my morning.

00:46:33.790 --> 00:46:36.200
Except going to the 15 AA meetings,

00:46:36.200 --> 00:46:38.113
I never even heard of that place,

00:46:39.460 --> 00:46:40.840
but I ended up on a mattress.

00:46:40.840 --> 00:46:42.640
I went out every night for eight years.

00:46:42.640 --> 00:46:44.600
I wake up on a mattress on the floor

00:46:44.600 --> 00:46:47.060
and it's three o'clock in the morning.

00:46:47.060 --> 00:46:48.720
The room is so dark.

00:46:48.720 --> 00:46:50.240
I can't even see my
hand in front of my face

00:46:50.240 --> 00:46:52.270
and there was no alcohol in the house.

00:46:52.270 --> 00:46:53.900
And I had the DTs.

00:46:53.900 --> 00:46:55.423
I'm shaking, I'm sweating.

00:46:56.940 --> 00:46:59.270
You know, my mind knows it's not real,

00:46:59.270 --> 00:47:02.060
but I can feel and see the devil.

00:47:02.060 --> 00:47:05.387
I say to this other body
next to me in the dark,

00:47:05.387 --> 00:47:07.890
"I think I'm gonna have
to go to the hospital."

00:47:07.890 --> 00:47:10.580
And they said, "Well, you're walking."

00:47:10.580 --> 00:47:14.737
And all of a sudden I heard
this voice in my ear saying,

00:47:14.737 --> 00:47:18.387
"Cassie, Cassie just quit."

00:47:19.900 --> 00:47:23.857
And it was like they were
speaking another language.

00:47:23.857 --> 00:47:24.690
"Just quit."

00:47:24.690 --> 00:47:27.670
Like, I never heard those
two words ever before.

00:47:27.670 --> 00:47:30.150
And this feeling of calm came over me.

00:47:30.150 --> 00:47:34.057
And I said to this other
human in the darkness,

00:47:34.057 --> 00:47:37.600
"I think I'm gonna go to
that AAAA place tomorrow."

00:47:37.600 --> 00:47:39.587
And they said, "Well, you're going alone."

00:47:40.800 --> 00:47:42.150
I looked it up the next day.

00:47:42.150 --> 00:47:43.930
And I went, and I took the burning desire.

00:47:43.930 --> 00:47:48.930
And I said, "Yes, some
would say I'm an alcoholic."

00:47:49.200 --> 00:47:51.637
Because in the beginning
of the meeting they ask,

00:47:51.637 --> 00:47:52.720
"Are you an alcoholic?"

00:47:52.720 --> 00:47:55.700
And I didn't respond.

00:47:55.700 --> 00:47:57.780
But at the end I said, "Yes, I am."

00:47:57.780 --> 00:48:00.003
And I didn't drink again for four years.

00:48:04.290 --> 00:48:05.940
I used to think God wants me bad.

00:48:09.860 --> 00:48:11.673
Yeah, I did that,

00:48:11.673 --> 00:48:13.973
then I decided to pick
up a cocaine addiction.

00:48:17.440 --> 00:48:19.980
I had been a cocaine
addict earlier in my life

00:48:20.860 --> 00:48:25.330
from one of the times
when my aunt needed money

00:48:25.330 --> 00:48:27.813
she sold me to the guy across the hall.

00:48:32.190 --> 00:48:34.390
He was probably in his first,

00:48:34.390 --> 00:48:37.223
in his second decade as
a serious coke addict.

00:48:38.500 --> 00:48:42.220
And I remember somebody
moving into the complex

00:48:42.220 --> 00:48:44.010
who turned out to be, his name was Randy.

00:48:44.010 --> 00:48:45.360
Randy turned out.

00:48:45.360 --> 00:48:47.740
He was an attorney that
had been disbarred.

00:48:47.740 --> 00:48:52.740
So he became a commercial real estate,

00:48:53.537 --> 00:48:57.190
no, industrial law, something like that.

00:48:57.190 --> 00:49:00.280
But somebody moved into the complex

00:49:00.280 --> 00:49:02.680
whom he went to college with.

00:49:02.680 --> 00:49:04.010
His wife had just left him.

00:49:04.010 --> 00:49:07.110
And I remember him taking
his first line of coke

00:49:07.110 --> 00:49:11.743
since college, six months
later he's carpet farming.

00:49:13.630 --> 00:49:16.210
He's in the carpet looking
for pieces of cocaine,

00:49:16.210 --> 00:49:19.083
which I now know he was looking for crack.

00:49:21.650 --> 00:49:26.610
And I had Michael, that first boyfriend,

00:49:26.610 --> 00:49:28.740
buy some cocaine for us.

00:49:28.740 --> 00:49:30.920
And he had never done cocaine.

00:49:30.920 --> 00:49:32.440
We were getting it every other day

00:49:32.440 --> 00:49:34.230
for the first three months.

00:49:34.230 --> 00:49:38.310
And I remember him looking up
at me after snorting a line

00:49:38.310 --> 00:49:43.310
off of that Radiohead CD, Pablo Honey

00:49:43.490 --> 00:49:45.960
and asking me, "Do I look cool?"

00:49:45.960 --> 00:49:47.480
And I said, "We're
never doing coke again."

00:49:47.480 --> 00:49:50.513
'Cause I remember that guy
crawling around on the carpet.

00:49:51.530 --> 00:49:53.780
I didn't want that kind
of blood on my hands.

00:49:54.740 --> 00:49:57.720
But after quitting the drinking

00:50:00.450 --> 00:50:02.410
I had a long way back.

00:50:02.410 --> 00:50:07.410
And I was barely there when
I got this pretty big job.

00:50:07.930 --> 00:50:11.233
And everyone thought I
was gonna fail at it.

00:50:12.740 --> 00:50:14.330
Around the same time a neighbor asked me

00:50:14.330 --> 00:50:16.850
if I knew where to get some cocaine.

00:50:16.850 --> 00:50:20.420
And I called a friend and
found out who delivered.

00:50:20.420 --> 00:50:22.273
And I decided to get myself a gram.

00:50:23.580 --> 00:50:25.143
Cocaine's an anesthetic.

00:50:26.220 --> 00:50:29.220
So I knew everything that was
happening, but I felt nothing.

00:50:30.220 --> 00:50:31.470
And that's what I wanted.

00:50:35.500 --> 00:50:36.509
During that period of time

00:50:36.509 --> 00:50:38.893
the inside of my nose fell out.

00:50:40.530 --> 00:50:45.530
So I was snorting about two grams a day,

00:50:46.630 --> 00:50:48.750
which went up to an eight ball.

00:50:48.750 --> 00:50:53.750
And for about a month,
I couldn't even breathe.

00:50:54.410 --> 00:50:56.660
I couldn't get more coke up my nose.

00:50:56.660 --> 00:50:59.520
Until one day something
came out of my nose

00:50:59.520 --> 00:51:01.733
and it was a chunk of
cartilage, basically.

00:51:05.950 --> 00:51:07.450
This is terrifying.

00:51:07.450 --> 00:51:10.100
I couldn't stop snorting
and my nose was falling out.

00:51:11.296 --> 00:51:13.070
A friend of mine, a DJ named Bizo

00:51:13.070 --> 00:51:16.377
went deaf and blind from his cocaine use.

00:51:20.410 --> 00:51:21.720
I didn't,

00:51:21.720 --> 00:51:24.360
also during the entire
time that I'm a coke addict

00:51:24.360 --> 00:51:27.120
I continued to go to AA meetings.

00:51:27.120 --> 00:51:28.470
I go late, I leave early.

00:51:28.470 --> 00:51:30.563
I sit in the back and say nothing.

00:51:32.690 --> 00:51:35.680
Not wanting to accept that I'm gonna be

00:51:35.680 --> 00:51:37.973
a cocaine addict always.

00:51:41.270 --> 00:51:45.423
So, I just felt so isolated, so alone.

00:51:48.470 --> 00:51:51.020
And I got a serious sinus infection,

00:51:51.020 --> 00:51:52.510
and I called my gynecologist,

00:51:52.510 --> 00:51:54.890
because he knew about my weight loss.

00:51:54.890 --> 00:51:59.720
And I flew back from San Francisco to,

00:51:59.720 --> 00:52:02.770
I was there for work, to see a specialist

00:52:02.770 --> 00:52:04.357
who never used the word cocaine, but said,

00:52:04.357 --> 00:52:07.420
"You need to stop the
medication immediately."

00:52:07.420 --> 00:52:09.163
And removed the inside of my nose.

00:52:12.330 --> 00:52:13.490
Okay, I'm just gonna say it.

00:52:13.490 --> 00:52:15.640
Around that time I met somebody,

00:52:15.640 --> 00:52:19.823
and it was a gated community in Calabasas.

00:52:20.700 --> 00:52:23.090
I was helping, he was recording an album.

00:52:23.090 --> 00:52:25.827
He had a giant bowl with all
these white chunks in it.

00:52:25.827 --> 00:52:28.220
And he said, "This isn't really ..."

00:52:28.220 --> 00:52:29.423
I hate the word crack.

00:52:31.040 --> 00:52:32.640
Why do they say crack
is a poor man's drug?

00:52:32.640 --> 00:52:34.020
This stuff, I mean, so basically,

00:52:34.020 --> 00:52:35.240
you take the stuff you get, right?

00:52:35.240 --> 00:52:36.080
And then you cook it.

00:52:36.080 --> 00:52:37.450
And then you only end up with half.

00:52:37.450 --> 00:52:38.283
I'm telling you.

00:52:42.300 --> 00:52:43.463
He smoked from a bong.

00:52:46.870 --> 00:52:47.703
I'll just say

00:52:47.703 --> 00:52:52.610
I would have some help from
some gentlemen friends.

00:52:53.960 --> 00:52:55.443
And some,

00:52:57.410 --> 00:53:00.143
we'll just stick to the
straight and narrow on this.

00:53:01.700 --> 00:53:04.610
Somebody introduced me
to him in the capacity of

00:53:06.880 --> 00:53:09.923
maybe we would hit it off to
enjoy an evening together.

00:53:10.790 --> 00:53:15.790
And I get to his home
and he's in a bathrobe.

00:53:16.540 --> 00:53:19.140
He's got cash in one
pocket, like Scarface,

00:53:19.140 --> 00:53:20.740
and gun in the other.

00:53:20.740 --> 00:53:24.963
And there's all these girls
around with really bad skin.

00:53:27.770 --> 00:53:30.010
There's contractors there
that are doing something,

00:53:30.010 --> 00:53:33.530
putting swirly cues on his windows.

00:53:33.530 --> 00:53:35.406
You know, a lot happening,

00:53:35.406 --> 00:53:37.473
what I now know is a
real crack head trait.

00:53:38.430 --> 00:53:40.903
Not because I'm a crack head or allegedly.

00:53:45.670 --> 00:53:47.670
I'm sorry, this is really uncomfortable.

00:53:49.510 --> 00:53:51.733
It's not like I lie, but by omission.

00:53:53.480 --> 00:53:55.080
But if you don't tell the truth,

00:53:57.130 --> 00:53:59.800
if you don't know where you stand,

00:53:59.800 --> 00:54:01.843
you don't know where you'll land, right?

00:54:04.150 --> 00:54:09.150
But yeah, this madam,
if you will, says, she,

00:54:10.630 --> 00:54:13.990
this is the third person
that I ever met through her.

00:54:13.990 --> 00:54:17.267
And she says, "Oh, you know,
don't expect, you know,

00:54:17.267 --> 00:54:20.957
"he's a party person, $100, $200."

00:54:24.750 --> 00:54:27.820
And we get there and he
asked me, "How much?"

00:54:27.820 --> 00:54:29.387
I said, "$1,000."

00:54:30.350 --> 00:54:32.120
And he looks at me up and down.

00:54:32.120 --> 00:54:33.940
He says, "Okay."

00:54:33.940 --> 00:54:36.000
He has her leave and closes the door.

00:54:36.000 --> 00:54:38.120
And then he says, "You're
not really a ho, are you?"

00:54:38.120 --> 00:54:39.440
And I was so embarrassed.

00:54:39.440 --> 00:54:42.070
I never heard anybody like use that word

00:54:42.070 --> 00:54:44.180
or like speak to me in that way.

00:54:44.180 --> 00:54:45.013
You know?

00:54:45.013 --> 00:54:47.533
I mean, like I said, I
lie to myself, you know?

00:54:48.620 --> 00:54:50.797
I was always arguing with my best friend,

00:54:50.797 --> 00:54:51.630
"There's a difference between

00:54:51.630 --> 00:54:52.720
"hamburger meat and filet mignon."

00:54:52.720 --> 00:54:55.137
And he says, "Prostitution
is prostitution."

00:54:56.160 --> 00:54:59.110
I guess I've come a long way
that I can even say that word.

00:55:01.520 --> 00:55:02.700
This is an unmarried guy.

00:55:02.700 --> 00:55:05.680
I mean, I carry around
so much shame about that.

00:55:05.680 --> 00:55:07.030
That's a whole other story.

00:55:09.350 --> 00:55:12.773
But that's how I learned about crack.

00:55:14.789 --> 00:55:17.697
And he was, but his first
statement was, "This isn't crack.

00:55:17.697 --> 00:55:19.307
"This is cocaine and I cook it."

00:55:20.410 --> 00:55:25.020
So it's cocaine, but isn't that crack?

00:55:25.020 --> 00:55:27.100
But anyway, we smoked from a bong.

00:55:27.100 --> 00:55:31.413
And he didn't have any
powder I could snort.

00:55:32.720 --> 00:55:35.240
It took me about a year before I started

00:55:35.240 --> 00:55:38.363
actually buying crack.

00:55:41.810 --> 00:55:43.710
I resent you for getting me to say it.

00:55:45.200 --> 00:55:46.400
No one got me to say it.

00:55:48.250 --> 00:55:49.203
My own free will.

00:55:50.095 --> 00:55:55.095
I only had one cocaine dealer.

00:55:55.330 --> 00:55:57.350
And he said to me, "I can get you hard."

00:55:57.350 --> 00:56:01.073
He never used the word
crack, just hard cocaine.

00:56:02.130 --> 00:56:04.500
And I mean, I guess in some
ways you could look at it like

00:56:04.500 --> 00:56:07.793
a blessing, because even if
I finally stopped snorting,

00:56:08.860 --> 00:56:10.450
cartilage still kept falling,

00:56:10.450 --> 00:56:12.163
still kept coming out of my nose.

00:56:14.933 --> 00:56:17.657
I could put a finger
all the way in the back

00:56:17.657 --> 00:56:20.507
and it would take a week for
whatever it was to come out.

00:56:22.580 --> 00:56:23.610
Wow.

00:56:23.610 --> 00:56:25.287
Wow, wow, wow.

00:56:28.470 --> 00:56:32.513
But yeah,

00:56:35.610 --> 00:56:37.533
so I started smoking crack.

00:56:39.250 --> 00:56:44.250
And I hid it from people,

00:56:44.860 --> 00:56:47.620
intuitively I needed
to hide it from people

00:56:47.620 --> 00:56:49.423
around that time, you know?

00:56:50.390 --> 00:56:53.563
I had too much money and too much grief.

00:56:55.580 --> 00:57:00.580
Pretty much self-indulgent
grief over some other things.

00:57:01.340 --> 00:57:03.543
So my dealer leaves a gram of heroin over.

00:57:04.600 --> 00:57:07.620
Shows me how to smoke it
although he didn't smoke it.

00:57:07.620 --> 00:57:09.773
And you know, I'll be darned if I didn't,

00:57:10.660 --> 00:57:12.140
it's really not that easy when

00:57:12.140 --> 00:57:13.820
you first start chasing the dragon.

00:57:13.820 --> 00:57:15.600
You've gotta roll up the tinfoil foil,

00:57:15.600 --> 00:57:18.580
you know, you've gotta kind
of point the tinfoil this way.

00:57:18.580 --> 00:57:20.763
I'm telling you, it's kind of difficult.

00:57:22.470 --> 00:57:25.550
But I got the hang of it and
just took on another addiction.

00:57:25.550 --> 00:57:27.700
So I was smoking two
grams of heroin a day.

00:57:28.780 --> 00:57:30.070
Besides the crack and then I found that

00:57:30.070 --> 00:57:31.923
bongs were not easy to transport.

00:57:35.130 --> 00:57:38.190
One day, my regular dealer is out of town.

00:57:38.190 --> 00:57:41.080
So we send somebody over
who comes with 30 packages

00:57:41.080 --> 00:57:42.760
all wrapped up in little squares.

00:57:42.760 --> 00:57:44.747
And I think, "Is what I'm gonna become?

00:57:44.747 --> 00:57:45.580
"Like what kind of drugs are you on

00:57:45.580 --> 00:57:47.837
"that you wrap these things
up in little squares?

00:57:47.837 --> 00:57:48.670
"What am I supposed to do with this?"

00:57:48.670 --> 00:57:49.993
I know now that's a dub,

00:57:51.370 --> 00:57:54.820
but that freaked me out so badly.

00:57:54.820 --> 00:57:55.860
I called my best friend.

00:57:55.860 --> 00:57:56.693
I gave him a number

00:57:56.693 --> 00:57:59.197
of somebody in AA and said,
"This is what's been happening.

00:57:59.197 --> 00:58:00.950
"I need to check myself in somewhere."

00:58:00.950 --> 00:58:02.983
Because I needed to want to want to quit.

00:58:04.884 --> 00:58:09.463
And in six hours I found
myself in this bougie rehab.

00:58:16.514 --> 00:58:20.673
I would say, let's bring this to today.

00:58:25.237 --> 00:58:27.623
If I'm honest, okay.

00:58:30.660 --> 00:58:35.660
I've always, I smoke heroin.

00:58:39.070 --> 00:58:40.863
I do cocaine.

00:58:47.960 --> 00:58:49.520
The last AA meeting I went to,

00:58:49.520 --> 00:58:51.640
which was seven years ago.

00:58:51.640 --> 00:58:53.337
I took the burning desire and said,

00:58:53.337 --> 00:58:55.577
"I know you got to have 24
hours before you can share,

00:58:55.577 --> 00:58:57.857
"but it's been five years.

00:58:57.857 --> 00:59:00.507
"So I'm just gonna say, you know,

00:59:00.507 --> 00:59:01.727
"I can't stop doing drugs

00:59:01.727 --> 00:59:03.972
"and my nose is falling out.

00:59:03.972 --> 00:59:06.972
"In my walk-in closet, that's
where I would go to try to ...

00:59:08.533 --> 00:59:10.747
"(indistinct)

00:59:10.747 --> 00:59:11.957
"It was so loud trying to blow my nose

00:59:11.957 --> 00:59:13.527
"or get whatever it was in there out.

00:59:13.527 --> 00:59:15.670
"And I think I'm gonna die."

00:59:15.670 --> 00:59:16.603
And I just left.

00:59:19.930 --> 00:59:22.047
Oh, I think I did say, "You
people set the bar so low

00:59:22.047 --> 00:59:23.347
"you could trip over it."

00:59:27.630 --> 00:59:29.250
The last conversation I
had with my little sister

00:59:29.250 --> 00:59:31.200
she asked me how I wanted to be buried.

00:59:33.710 --> 00:59:35.710
She's never even seen me do these drugs.

00:59:41.470 --> 00:59:43.193
I started, anyway.

00:59:46.046 --> 00:59:50.470
You know, I always thought
that if I ever asked for help

00:59:50.470 --> 00:59:51.950
that it would be there,

00:59:51.950 --> 00:59:53.700
that I'd been paying into that.

00:59:53.700 --> 00:59:54.893
I never cried wolf.

00:59:58.640 --> 01:00:02.530
And it's kind of like seeing
a fire extinguisher every day.

01:00:02.530 --> 01:00:04.080
And not only when you break the glass

01:00:04.080 --> 01:00:06.130
do you realize that it's empty,

01:00:06.130 --> 01:00:07.740
it's not even a real fire extinguisher.

01:00:07.740 --> 01:00:09.683
It's like a blow up fire extinguisher.

01:00:15.221 --> 01:00:16.640
When I was in, had been an alcoholic

01:00:17.620 --> 01:00:21.473
I sought out help for that,

01:00:22.630 --> 01:00:24.093
looking for a facility.

01:00:24.940 --> 01:00:28.217
They were quoting me $30,000, $50,000.

01:00:28.217 --> 01:00:31.550
And now mind you, it was a
little bit of a different time.

01:00:31.550 --> 01:00:33.823
And also you need round the clock care.

01:00:34.910 --> 01:00:37.370
So I didn't know anything about

01:00:37.370 --> 01:00:40.020
some place that was free or
something of that nature.

01:00:41.993 --> 01:00:43.980
And I thought every rehab was that,

01:00:43.980 --> 01:00:47.800
I didn't know it was mostly
indigenous to just alcohol.

01:00:47.800 --> 01:00:51.760
So I go to this rehab.

01:00:51.760 --> 01:00:52.979
It was a horrible experience.

01:00:52.979 --> 01:00:56.757
One of the facilitators calling
me in her office and saying,

01:00:56.757 --> 01:01:00.167
"You know, if you want to dress
like that every single day,

01:01:00.167 --> 01:01:01.477
"you know, that's fine.

01:01:01.477 --> 01:01:03.860
"But if you just want
to be seen as you know,

01:01:04.912 --> 01:01:08.197
"so when it's, you know, just shallow

01:01:08.197 --> 01:01:13.197
"and is just good for nothing
but being on somebody's arm.

01:01:13.547 --> 01:01:15.727
"I mean, that's fine, that's up to you.

01:01:15.727 --> 01:01:16.827
"You know, just because we don't have

01:01:16.827 --> 01:01:18.537
"600 thread count sheets here

01:01:18.537 --> 01:01:20.850
"doesn't mean that we can't help you."

01:01:20.850 --> 01:01:22.420
And I am so ...

01:01:22.420 --> 01:01:23.980
I was sitting there.

01:01:23.980 --> 01:01:26.510
I'm so exhausted.

01:01:26.510 --> 01:01:28.320
I didn't ...

01:01:28.320 --> 01:01:30.853
This is what this woman is saying to me.

01:01:32.460 --> 01:01:33.293
You know?

01:01:34.370 --> 01:01:38.700
I mean, I called in maybe
the only favor I ever had

01:01:38.700 --> 01:01:42.450
in my life to get this like $32,000

01:01:42.450 --> 01:01:44.300
to get to this place to realize

01:01:44.300 --> 01:01:46.490
I'm the only one that paid any money

01:01:46.490 --> 01:01:48.380
and they have these scholarships

01:01:48.380 --> 01:01:51.780
and they're also charging my
insurance $10,000 a month.

01:01:51.780 --> 01:01:54.483
And she's talking to me
about thread count on sheets.

01:01:55.570 --> 01:01:57.890
Come to find out that
the guy, Chris Bathum,

01:01:57.890 --> 01:02:00.680
was arrested three years later for

01:02:00.680 --> 01:02:03.030
possession and insurance fraud.

01:02:03.030 --> 01:02:03.863
Yeah.

01:02:05.500 --> 01:02:08.420
I ended up losing two Mac computers

01:02:08.420 --> 01:02:11.853
and my iPhone and my hard drive.

01:02:13.620 --> 01:02:16.240
Some little boy toy I had
been fooling around with

01:02:16.240 --> 01:02:18.500
put a security pin on my phone.

01:02:18.500 --> 01:02:23.077
So that payment couldn't
be accepted for my phone.

01:02:25.260 --> 01:02:29.120
And I was there one day prior to 90.

01:02:29.120 --> 01:02:31.563
So I lost the phone
number I had for 15 years.

01:02:33.170 --> 01:02:34.870
I think I had mentioned a little bit

01:02:34.870 --> 01:02:39.870
about having had mentors or gentlemen that

01:02:39.947 --> 01:02:44.433
helped greatly financially in my life.

01:02:46.840 --> 01:02:51.680
So the loss of me not
being able to call out,

01:02:51.680 --> 01:02:53.430
my phone not being able to call in.

01:02:56.920 --> 01:02:59.893
Yeah, it was of epic proportions.

01:03:03.392 --> 01:03:07.560
And after, basically I lost everything.

01:03:07.560 --> 01:03:09.743
So after I fled from that place.

01:03:10.700 --> 01:03:12.800
Ooh, people were so, I gotta tell you,

01:03:12.800 --> 01:03:14.170
people were pretty thrilled that

01:03:14.170 --> 01:03:16.370
now maybe Cassie will
be off her high horse.

01:03:18.620 --> 01:03:20.920
I didn't know I was on
such high hours really.

01:03:24.210 --> 01:03:29.180
And come to find out my
dealer's been sent away

01:03:29.180 --> 01:03:31.493
on a mandatory vacation in jail.

01:03:32.660 --> 01:03:33.740
Of course, as soon as I got out

01:03:33.740 --> 01:03:35.180
the first thing I wanted to do was use,

01:03:35.180 --> 01:03:37.580
but I had learned some
stuff in rehab about cavy

01:03:38.500 --> 01:03:42.410
and what words to use and
possibly how to go to score

01:03:42.410 --> 01:03:43.860
which I had been ignorant of.

01:03:46.050 --> 01:03:47.320
I gave up my apartment

01:03:48.880 --> 01:03:52.150
to go to this place

01:03:52.150 --> 01:03:54.490
thinking I needed a whole fresh new start.

01:03:54.490 --> 01:03:55.700
So when I get out,

01:03:55.700 --> 01:03:57.750
I ended up staying with an old boyfriend.

01:03:59.130 --> 01:04:01.860
But I go down,

01:04:01.860 --> 01:04:05.850
I started to travel down
towards the Skid Row area.

01:04:05.850 --> 01:04:08.773
And I think I had like
150 bucks in my pocket.

01:04:16.170 --> 01:04:17.517
I'm a bit of (indistinct).

01:04:18.780 --> 01:04:20.660
But I get to Alvarado.

01:04:20.660 --> 01:04:22.270
They looked at me like I'm crazy.

01:04:22.270 --> 01:04:26.200
By the time I get down to
Fifth and Broadway, you know,

01:04:27.865 --> 01:04:29.227
I mean, I think this is just
the most horrible place,

01:04:29.227 --> 01:04:31.680
and this is as far as I've ever been.

01:04:31.680 --> 01:04:33.990
But now I'm down to what, like $60?

01:04:33.990 --> 01:04:36.310
Because I'm giving someone
10 bucks to show me where

01:04:36.310 --> 01:04:37.308
like the dub is.

01:04:37.308 --> 01:04:39.933
I don't know if it's dub, dub, you know?

01:04:40.940 --> 01:04:44.067
And I see, I meet this guy and he says,

01:04:44.067 --> 01:04:45.237
"You know, I don't use drugs anymore,

01:04:45.237 --> 01:04:48.660
"but you're gonna need a line,
I'll show you where it is."

01:04:48.660 --> 01:04:52.203
So it's a foggy memory, but
he takes me down to Skid Row.

01:04:54.299 --> 01:04:55.820
I score some drugs.

01:04:55.820 --> 01:04:58.823
And which, I think I had
money enough for a dime.

01:05:00.830 --> 01:05:03.273
He waits for me outside of
his tent that he allowed,

01:05:03.273 --> 01:05:07.910
that he, I guess rented for
me so I can smoke my heroin,

01:05:07.910 --> 01:05:10.000
and gets on the bus with me.

01:05:10.000 --> 01:05:12.000
And he's an African-American man.

01:05:12.000 --> 01:05:13.890
I never dated a black man before.

01:05:13.890 --> 01:05:15.500
I never really had any experience of that.

01:05:15.500 --> 01:05:18.017
But he pulls some money
out of his pocket and says,

01:05:18.017 --> 01:05:22.700
"Oh, I'm for real, can I
get your phone number?"

01:05:22.700 --> 01:05:25.300
And it was kind of awkward
and kind of gauche,

01:05:25.300 --> 01:05:28.336
but also boyish and sweet.

01:05:28.336 --> 01:05:32.607
And I look at him and I think,

01:05:32.607 --> 01:05:35.677
"Man, you know, I really don't want to

01:05:35.677 --> 01:05:38.240
"get the esoteric check for this one."

01:05:38.240 --> 01:05:41.240
I think he must be like 26 years old.

01:05:41.240 --> 01:05:43.240
Come to find out he was much older, but.

01:05:46.220 --> 01:05:49.163
I said I would take his
number and consider it.

01:05:51.420 --> 01:05:53.560
Well, it was on and cracking, you know?

01:05:53.560 --> 01:05:58.550
So I started smoking crack and, ah,

01:05:58.550 --> 01:05:59.520
and smoking heroin,

01:05:59.520 --> 01:06:01.320
and now I'm not in my own place anymore.

01:06:01.320 --> 01:06:04.170
The delivery guy isn't there, you know?

01:06:04.170 --> 01:06:06.793
The left hand suddenly knows
what the right hand is doing.

01:06:10.360 --> 01:06:12.325
Long story short, Andrew
comes back to catch me

01:06:12.325 --> 01:06:15.173
in bed with another man.

01:06:18.910 --> 01:06:21.250
Me and Andrew, I don't know, wow,

01:06:21.250 --> 01:06:25.113
that sounded so much less
embarrassing in my head.

01:06:26.630 --> 01:06:28.340
Ah, man.

01:06:28.340 --> 01:06:31.000
Mind you, we were not
boyfriend-girlfriend,

01:06:31.000 --> 01:06:33.730
but I do think there's really,

01:06:33.730 --> 01:06:36.380
that's goes against Miss Manners for sure.

01:06:36.380 --> 01:06:37.980
And that it really is not,

01:06:37.980 --> 01:06:42.550
and it's not a good thing,
good or bad thing, bad.

01:06:42.550 --> 01:06:44.480
Yeah, not good, not good.

01:06:44.480 --> 01:06:48.030
So I ended up calling
this person that I met

01:06:48.030 --> 01:06:51.453
and he comes and rescues me.

01:06:54.880 --> 01:06:58.210
And I started, I'm staying at a hotel.

01:06:58.210 --> 01:07:01.120
Like not quite a crack hotel,

01:07:01.120 --> 01:07:03.973
but like a really crappy hotel.

01:07:04.878 --> 01:07:06.920
You know, I mean,

01:07:06.920 --> 01:07:09.377
I used to stay at the
Bristol in Paris, right?

01:07:12.951 --> 01:07:15.643
This is for reference, come on, you know?

01:07:20.174 --> 01:07:22.540
You know, that was a billion mile fall.

01:07:22.540 --> 01:07:25.140
People have been waiting
for this billion mile fall.

01:07:26.100 --> 01:07:27.850
I ended up following him down here.

01:07:28.850 --> 01:07:33.850
And I was in the first
week of being down here.

01:07:35.160 --> 01:07:38.900
He gave me a black eye,
almost knocked me out cold.

01:07:38.900 --> 01:07:40.400
I thought a plane had fallen,

01:07:40.400 --> 01:07:42.810
I went through the roof.

01:07:42.810 --> 01:07:43.820
It was nine in the morning.

01:07:43.820 --> 01:07:46.510
And what hurt the most
was I was smiling at him.

01:07:46.510 --> 01:07:48.610
He said, he thought I was laughing at him.

01:07:50.710 --> 01:07:51.990
He had been sober when I met him,

01:07:51.990 --> 01:07:55.943
but quickly started smoking crack with me.

01:07:57.350 --> 01:07:59.850
So I found a place to hide out

01:07:59.850 --> 01:08:02.720
and I felt I was trying to decide

01:08:02.720 --> 01:08:04.070
if I wanted to live or die.

01:08:06.040 --> 01:08:08.890
And it's kinda been Shawshank
Redemption time ever since.

01:08:10.172 --> 01:08:11.482
I feel embarrassed about the whole thing.

01:08:11.482 --> 01:08:12.640
And I felt like it was the last place

01:08:12.640 --> 01:08:14.300
anyone would ever look for me.

01:08:14.300 --> 01:08:16.250
And I thought I could fix it by myself.

01:08:18.810 --> 01:08:20.913
And I'll end it with this.

01:08:23.320 --> 01:08:24.177
People always say,

01:08:24.177 --> 01:08:26.210
"God never gives you more
than anything you can handle."

01:08:26.210 --> 01:08:27.370
Right?

01:08:27.370 --> 01:08:29.570
I think you were saying
something like that.

01:08:31.552 --> 01:08:34.183
So to my understanding the
crux of the Bible is free will.

01:08:36.130 --> 01:08:37.280
This might seem like a non-sequitur,

01:08:37.280 --> 01:08:42.099
but in any language, on any
planet, in any vampire story,

01:08:42.099 --> 01:08:46.490
a vampire cannot enter
unless they ask permission.

01:08:46.490 --> 01:08:49.073
So that's the front and
the back of the matter.

01:08:51.000 --> 01:08:53.250
The only thing that I've figured out

01:08:53.250 --> 01:08:57.973
from these last, and it's, I have been,

01:08:59.910 --> 01:09:01.963
I saw this over two-and-a-half years ago.

01:09:03.850 --> 01:09:05.863
If I lied about it, I apologize.

01:09:07.470 --> 01:09:10.440
I mean, I've done things since then.

01:09:10.440 --> 01:09:11.810
This is all so embarrassing.

01:09:11.810 --> 01:09:14.940
But the only thing I've learned is that

01:09:16.160 --> 01:09:18.910
manners are the most
important thing to me.

01:09:18.910 --> 01:09:22.127
And also that I really didn't
need to learn this lesson.

